I’m a designer, not a professional developer, but working side by side with developers has taught me a thing or two, and with Cline as my AI assistant in VS Code, I built this site myself. I did the visual design in Figma, brought the designs to life in code, and keep refining the site as the campaign moves along.

I made sure the site stays consistent as it grows: colors and fonts are defined as variables, and recurring elements are built as global components, so there are no hard-coded styles to hunt down later.

Our team’s expertise came in handy during the build too. Among other things, the site includes Google Analytics, a newsletter embed and an Instagram feed embed. To keep the content easy to update, I added Keystatic as a content management tool, so new pages and articles can be published without touching the code. GitHub and Cloudflare take care of publishing.

This project shows how AI-assisted development can bring a designer closer to the finished product. The design ends up on the live site as intended, and I can fix and polish the details directly.
